00downloads/README
2023-Aug-25

This directory contains the downloads for Theory of Computation by Jim Hefferon.
Probably you want book.pdf containing the full electronic version.

In the book a few of the diagrams can be animated or have opacity.
Some PDF readers don't support these.  So while reading the book works
perfectly well without these features, you may want to consider another reader.
I know that Acrobat Reader supports them and there may be others. 

Also here is the Answers to Exercises for the book, answers.pdf.  If you put
the book and the answers in the same directory then clicking on any of the
book's exercise numbers will take you to the associated answer, and clicking
on the answer number takes you back to the exercise.

Finally, slides.zip contains the in-class slides that I used when teaching
the class.


HOME PAGE

More on this text and my others is at https://hefferon.net. 


LICENSE

The license is that you can use these materials either for self-study or
for a class you are teaching.  In particular, you can put a copy on a
class's LMS for students to download.  For a complete statement see 
https://hefferon.net/source.html.


PAPER VERSION

See https://hefferon.net/computation/hardcopy.html. 